  "problem": "Calculate the minor of the entry ${d}_{23}$ in the matrix\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -12 & 44 & -33 \\\\ 25 & 30 & 41\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "The minor of ${d}_{23}=-33$ (second row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-33$ are removed: \n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217 & -33 \\\\ 25 & 30 & \u2217\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${d}_{23}=-33$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 25 & 30\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 25 & 30\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10\\cdot 30-2\\cdot 25 \\\\  & =300-50 \\\\  & =250.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
